= A Senator from Vermont

A democratic socialist senator from Vermont announces he will seek the Democratic nomination. Crowds are bigger than anyone expected. The establishment has a plan to coronate a front-runner. The question is how to treat the insurgency.

- @neutral: Insist on a neutral, open primary.
- @establishment: Quietly back the front-runner.
- @absorb: Invite the insurgents into the platform process.

@neutral
subtitle: Fairer, riskier.
on-arrival: dnc_neutral = 1; prog_dissent -= 5; unity += 2; prog_strength += 3; nominee_mod += 0

We promise a level field. The left believes us, mostly.

@establishment
subtitle: Safer in the short run, corrosive later.
on-arrival: dnc_neutral = 0; estab_strength += 2; prog_dissent += 6; far_left += 2

The party apparatus lines up behind the front-runner. It is not a secret.

@absorb
subtitle: Co-opts energy.
on-arrival: prog_dissent -= 3; unity += 2; mod_dissent += 2; prog_strength += 2

We give their ideas a seat at the table. Some call it co-optation. Others call it politics.
